  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive: the thing liked takes が, not ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ — ⟦この→この：00962_kono⟧⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{気|き}に{入|い}った. The person who likes it is the topic (⟦{私|わたし}→私：02988_watashi⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦この→この：00962_kono⟧⟦{服|ふく}→服：00695_fuku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{気|き}に{入|い}った) or is simply left out.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {気|き}に{入|い}った: took a liking to it — said on first seeing or receiving something\n- {気|き}に{入|い}って⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧: likes it, is fond of it — the continuing state, for something one has had a while\n\nFORMS:\n- {気|き}に{入|い}らない: not to like; also to find annoying (⟦あの→あの：00915_ano⟧⟦{態度|たいど}→態度：03396_taido⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{気|き}に{入|い}らない)\n- ⟦お{気|き}に{入|い}り→お気に入り：10297_okiniiri⟧: favorite (noun) — ⟦お{気|き}に{入|い}り→お気に入り：10297_okiniiri⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{店|みせ}→店：00497_mise⟧\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{好|す}き→好き：02355_suki⟧: like — a lasting preference; {気|き}に{入|い}る is liking something one has just met or received",
